-- title:
--   A three-torsion projection from a character
-- statement:
--   Let $G$ be an abelian group. Let $\chi:G\to\mathbb Z/3$ be additive and $a,d,h\in G$ satisfy $2h=0$, $3d\in\{0,h\}$, and $\chi(a)=\chi(h)=0$, $\chi(d)=1$. There is an additive endomorphism $p$ with $$p^2=p,\quad 3p(x)=0\ (x\in G),\quad p(a)=p(h)=0,\quad p(d)=-2d.$$
--
--   This constructs the idempotent needed for reflection.
